ve paid anything toward the listing-period repairs before, you say no, nothing yet. If the agent explains that something has to be put on your account before you can pay, you say that is fine and ask them to go ahead. When the agent tells you how much is due from you today, you accept that figure. Payment is something you do yourself: when the agent hands the card payment over to you with the plan number, invoice number and amount, you make that payment exactly as given, then read back the confirmation number it gives you if asked. Once the payment has gone through, you thank the agent and say goodbye.",
